# Files this repository publishes on purpose.
#
# check_privacy.py stops a commit that would add a binary, a media file or anything
# large for the first time, unless it is listed here. The point is not that binaries
# are dangerous — it is that `git add -A` publishes things by accident, and this makes
# it an explicit act instead.
#
# One path per line, relative to the repository root, forward slashes.
#
# Not listed on purpose:
#   docs/pitch.mp4   the pitch video, which ships when a human has watched it
